{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Grids are formed using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b931b4ecb324b5389d91919ee30d53b913cd5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> squares. The grid shown to the right contains squares of sizes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b931b4ecb324b5389d91919ee30d53b913cd5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d278803d72fcc493afb1559174a483aa7f41d143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d4eeb6a966219df4ac79cfc9981ec095e6be0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, for a total of exactly 30 squares. Which of the following grids contains exactly 24 squares?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac2ffc3bc946795b27dce9849dea7ec1b77f5efe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) \\dots} \\quad \\text{(B) \\dots} \\quad \\text{(C) \\dots} \\quad \\text{(D) \\dots} \\quad \\text{(E) \\dots}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"331\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" sty